    {
      "id": "claim_1ecd2c946c014a26884364f7b16e0ccd",
      "statement": "TelegramGatewayService serializes pollers with a per-token filesystem lease: the lock file is named by the first 16 hex chars of sha256(token) under DJIMIT_TELEGRAM_LEASE_DIR or os.tmpdir()/djimit-telegram-leases, created atomically with fs.openSync 'wx', carries a JSON payload of machineId/name/hostId/pid/startedAt, has a 2-minute TTL, and is kept fresh by a 30-second unref'd heartbeat that refreshes mtimes of all held leases.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/telegram/src/index.ts#L26-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4f3e1449dee5bfdb85a13788bffbc0be057f5aae5c9aaa72fac9eb25b2ce14b4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/telegram/src/index.ts#L47-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:68248d267b5ea9dcbdc6aef9f25461313ccd3ed6893bb2867a4e64f77c45b5a1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_898223366c4b4d65a2a648bc480dc3ec",
      "statement": "On EEXIST the lease is reclaimed only through two tiers: a host-qualified dead-pid probe (same recorded host and process.kill(pid,0) raising ESRCH, with EPERM treated as alive so a live owner on the same host is never taken over and cross-host pid probes are skipped), or TTL expiry applied regardless of host or payload readability so a truncated lease from a crashed writer cannot wedge polling; an ENOENT between EEXIST and statSync is retried as a release race.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/telegram/src/index.test.ts#L85-L162",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a2e52a3c8f8a966d7835b7e8957214c6ef32b21597fbab1af12c6fb576a049b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/telegram/src/index.ts#L64-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7a2af64f09295fdae2feaec409686283148bffa68d9d4968b29199e7418d9eb0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d688765bac174fbcbf54af2301dd600f",
      "statement": "When lease acquisition fails, startAll retries with 2s/5s/15s/30s/60s backoff to ride out overlapping restarts and then skips that bot with a warning; per-bot init failure removes that bot's lease, and stopAll clears the heartbeat, settles every bot.stop(), and unlinks all held leases. The server retains the gateway and calls stopAll() in the SIGTERM handler specifically so a restart does not see EEXIST and skip polling forever.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/index.ts#L335-L337",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4451c83a2bd7e3da2c0a891c453182feef1cc1dccf25a6483a4ae5a4bc71b58c:"
