    {
      "id": "claim_a746baa41ba94a48bf0dc1b5577b694a",
      "statement": "A grammY middleware in the gateway enforces authorization before any command handler: the sender id must be present, be in the bot config's allowedUsers, and map through userMap to a non-blank actor string, otherwise the update is answered with '⛔ Telegram user is not authorized and linked to a DjimFlo account.' and dropped — the code comments that a bot token identifies the transport, never the requesting user.",
      "evidence": [
