    {
      "id": "claim_9297ca428320423f8b429a9eb631224d",
      "statement": "TelegramApiService's createTask/getStatus/cancelTask arrow-function fields are exactly the ops shape consumed by TelegramGatewayService: createTask posts a pending local-execution task tagged 'telegram' with the machineId in metadata and returns its id, getStatus counts visible active/pending tasks for that machineId, and cancelTask posts to /tasks/:id/cancel — so both Telegram surfaces funnel mutations into the same authenticated REST/approval spine.",
