    {
      "id": "claim_bc0cd7c5f19c4e908421f1bce2cb72ad",
      "statement": "The end-to-end chain test proves the ownership and governance invariants for Telegram-created work: an allowed sender's /task lands as a pending task owned and created_by the mapped user with a task.created audit event, the owner cannot self-approve (SELF_APPROVAL_FORBIDDEN), a viewer-role user gets FORBIDDEN, approval by an approver-role user lets mock execution complete, only the owner can cancel a running task, and unknown, unlinked, disabled, or downgraded senders create zero tasks.",
